From e49a4c9ca0eeeee2261fc14c8a12d365dcaeaaff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:51:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/36] code, overlays: write the search loops with their exit
 test in the header
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`while (true) { if (!c) break; … }` where the test is the first statement
is `while (c) { … }`: audio_load.c's DMA chunk loop (`size >= 0x400`),
z_jpeg.c (`!exit`), the two map-mark walks (`markType != NONE`), the two
digit loops in z_file_choose.c (`*ones >= 100` / `>= 10` — an s16
promoted to int, so `(*ones - 100) < 0` is exactly `*ones < 100`),
Bg_Spot16_Bombstone's table walk (De Morgan on integer tests, bounds
check still first), and code_800EC960.c's `while (f()) {}`. z_eff_blure.c's
`if (c) { … } else { break; }` is the same inversion.

Verified: every file compiles to byte-identical assembly before and
after with the port's own flags (asmdiff over compile_commands.json).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 soh/src/code/audio_load.c                                   | 5 +----
 soh/src/code/code_800EC960.c                                | 5 +----
 soh/src/code/z_jpeg.c                                       | 6 +-----
 soh/src/code/z_map_mark.c                                   | 6 +-----
 .../actors/ovl_Bg_Spot16_Bombstone/z_bg_spot16_bombstone.c  | 6 +-----
 soh/src/overlays/misc/ovl_kaleido_scope/z_lmap_mark.c       | 6 +-----
 6 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/audio_load.c b/soh/src/code/audio_load.c
index f5b52a105..5802d246f 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/audio_load.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/audio_load.c
@@ -949,10 +949,7 @@ void AudioLoad_SyncDma(uintptr_t devAddr, u8* addr, size_t size, s32 medium) {
 
     Audio_InvalDCache(addr, size);
 
-    while (true) {
-        if (size < 0x400) {
-            break;
-        }
+    while (size >= 0x400) {
         AudioLoad_Dma(ioMesg, OS_MESG_PRI_HIGH, OS_READ, devAddr, addr, 0x400, msgQueue, medium, "FastCopy");
         osRecvMesg(msgQueue, NULL, OS_MESG_BLOCK);
         size -= 0x400;
